<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rio Grande do Norte</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> do Norte is a state in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> on the Atlantic coast, at the north-eastern corner of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, with its capital at Natal. Colonised by the Portuguese from 1598, when the Fort of the Three Kings was built at Natal, it was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> from 1633 to 1654. Its economy long rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and salt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rio-grande-do-norte.jpg" alt="Rio Grande do Norte" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giro720 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandeira_do_Rio_Grande_do_Norte.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
